1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,733
What happens when market signals and company filings disagree?

2
00:00:04,733 --> 00:00:09,533
CONTRA puts independent evidence and investor limits in one explainable view.

3
00:00:09,933 --> 00:00:16,200
Three agents inspect a frozen snapshot. Every conclusion links back to its
source.

4
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:22,467
Choose ALPHA.NS, a clearly labeled synthetic scenario with known outcomes.

5
00:00:22,467 --> 00:00:28,667
The Conservative profile has a 10 percent single asset cap. Now run the
analysis.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:35,867
Price momentum is positive. Filing evidence is negative. The result is
conflicted.

7
00:00:35,867 --> 00:00:41,000
CONTRA sizes the action from this investor's holdings and risk cap.

8
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:46,666
Click a cited reason to inspect the exact frozen filing excerpt and its date.

9
00:00:46,666 --> 00:00:52,533
The report also records three concurrent agent intervals and their execution
modes.

10
00:00:52,533 --> 00:00:59,200
The fourth dimension separates foreign and domestic flows. These figures are
synthetic market context.

11
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:04,533
Now compare all three investors using the exact same market snapshot.

12
00:01:04,533 --> 00:01:11,333
Conservative trims, Growth holds, and Starter stays out. The evidence is
unchanged.

13
00:01:11,333 --> 00:01:17,733
Ask the filings about operating margin. The answer is an exact stored passage.

14
00:01:17,733 --> 00:01:23,733
When no excerpt supports a question, CONTRA abstains instead of guessing.

15
00:01:23,733 --> 00:01:29,067
Evaluation checks scenarios, citation integrity and measured execution.

16
00:01:29,067 --> 00:01:35,067
CONTRA is research software. It does not predict returns or execute trades.

17
00:01:35,067 --> 00:01:40,067
Explore the working demo and inspect the public source code.
